module gunbc.heal_repair_declaration

import std.types { String }

// THE PATH IS DECLARED ONCE AND CONSUMED BY BOTH ENDS. The generated-artifact gate WRITES this file
// and the heal commit step READS it; if each spelled its own literal the two would drift and the
// failure would be silent -- heal would commit with no trailer and nothing would say the declaration
// had been written somewhere nobody looked. It lives under target/ because that directory is ignored,
// so the declaration cannot itself become a committed artifact the drift gate then has to adjudicate.
//
// It lives in its own module rather than beside the trailer renderer in gunbc.ledger_row_coherence
// because that module reads the ledger rosters, and heal reading one path must not put every ledger
// row in its closure: a ledger row is a design record, not an input to heal.
data heal_repair_declaration_artifact_path: String = "target/heal-repair-declaration.txt"
